ontext failure, refuse Ready and dispose the actual context/browser; late launch completion after stop is disposed too. The parent bounds or forces process-tree teardown and scratch/capacity release. Never swallow startup cleanup failure, choose a stray recording or wait indefinitely for native video. Parent/child start and absolute admission/run deadlines continue across every startup step and cleanup; neither page replacement nor clock sampling resets or extends them. Sample the existing paired wall/monotonic run origin once at clean application-page recording readiness, validate its blank world before Ready, and retain measured pinned-recorder seek calibration. Clean app-page readiness is established before the existing one-time paired origin sample and blank-world/liveness check before Ready. An application recording may have a measured bounded blank prefix; actual pinned native-recorder calibration must still meet the existing controlled-fixture seek target within 500 ms for initial navigation and failure. No diagnostic-prefix arithmetic or virtual timing result substitutes for decoded native video or outstanding staging calibration. Keep the existing admitted runtime budget/window and continuous absolute run/parent deadlines; do not grant a new runtime allowance on page replacement. Only this application page supplies native app video; no rewrite, merge, transcode, diagnostic-prefix subtraction or altered application recording is allowed. Native partial/evidence state remains determined by actual application recording finalization, independently of outcome. Guided unrecorded startup currently stays unchanged; OBS-013 must record the same sole clean application page in its existing guided context. This sequential trusted bootstrap exception does not permit popups, multi-page application workflows, extra contexts, browser modes, arguments, sandbox bypass, new wire fields or image-provenance waiver. Backend resolution may already precede launch; this rule makes n